      "id": "M04",
      "page": 125,
      "location": "After Listing 2, before comparison paragraph",
      "kind": "insert_before",
      "before": "Further operations are needed for the sake of Turing completeness so next comparison is considered.",
      "after": "OP64 and USEWORDOP64 apply operations to corresponding 32-bit halves. Their MOV, XOR, AND, OR and NOT forms have the corresponding whole-word meaning; in OP64's immediate form, data is replicated in both halves. Independent half-word ADD or SUB gives whole-word arithmetic only when carry or borrow is absent; otherwise it must be propagated. DWORD helpers restore EAX; in 64-bit mode their final RAX is the zero extension of EAX. Full RAX restoration assumes a zero-extended entry RAX."
    },
